• Pay bills and maintain ledgers; Receive, approve, and/or decline invoices; Code payables for accounts payable entries; Conduct invoice activities and pay vendors; 
• Assist with budget preparations; Responsible for monitoring the flow of cash into and out of an organization; Making reasonable suggestion of Line of Credit transfers when funding is needed for different projects that the organization is working on; 
• Make bank deposits and receipts of money; making sure the corresponding team finishes the reconciliations and fix any discrepancies; 
• Preparing the commission reports and processing payroll; Generate GL reports and other payroll reports; 
• Create and maintain multiple reports through Quickbooks and Sage Timeslips for the firm; 
• Analyze business operations, trends, costs, revenues, financial commitments, and obligations, to project future revenues and expenses or to provide advice.

education.description:
This Diploma gives understanding in the field of macro-phenomena, national and international economic, civil and tax legislation, systems and business processes, tools, marketing, and financial products. Integrates professional expertise with specific language and computer skills to work in the company's information system and to both contribute to its innovation and to its organizational and technological improving.
The student is able to:
Establish business operations using methods, tools, accounting techniques and other in line with the national and international principles;
Draw and interpret corporate financial and administrative documents;
Manage compliance of a fiscal nature;
Collaborate with contract negotiations related to the different functional areas of the company;
Collaborate in the organization, control and management and of business processes;
Use software and applications for the integrated management of the accounting, finance and marketing.

